  "status_text": "Today's question, in plain words: how much can flipping signals from yes to no ever save? Several families of graphs now carry a checked saving that grows with their size, at least 2n - 7 gates on each, and the bet still open on the desk says no graph can save more than 2n - 5 [L-meta-19158, L-meta-19159, both conjectures]. One graph that saves more breaks it; a proof makes 2n - 5 the exact limit on one-a-side inputs. Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
